{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787956864593704401,"compiled_state":{"alias":"resistant-constant-nurseshark","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"deef7258ceb540d6cb9585db0676bebcc173a4ecf7d930aa5f1b106cb148d32b","event_uuid":"acd534df-7330-4db8-9066-ea95107b5d5e","position":{"commit_sha":"53fb671991e03051e2b1c33335dc1346706f04a3","position":"1787956828802163990-acd534df-7330-4db8-9066-ea95107b5d5e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"5bdc9afb3ee6b23617e786f57cf9ebfa6941ee254abe2fa7f94785c0478a0f2d","event_uuid":"ed7cc4a4-a4fa-4303-ab98-41500b5f3ba7","position":{"commit_sha":"5ccf815793f145a07496f3ac1a3d2fd266b4014f","position":"1787956864593704400-ed7cc4a4-a4fa-4303-ab98-41500b5f3ba7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787956828802163990,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe lean discovery row is not lean. `include_body=False` drops only `description` and\n`comments`, leaving four base64 DSSE signature fields in every row. Measured on this store\n(2,855 tickets) those four are **88% of a \"lean\" list's bytes** — `authorship_ledger`\n26,241,422 B (59%), `attestations` 10,370,251 B (23%), `signature` 2,639,114 B (6%) — so a\nlean list is 44,392,067 B and 15,548 B/row. Dropping them gives 4,928,872 B and 1,726 B/row,\na 9x reduction.\n\nA list caller is choosing a ticket. The signature record is read per-ticket via `show` /\n`verify-signature`, which are untouched. Two backends spell the lean row separately today\n(`_engine_support/reads.py::list_states` and `_snapshot/ticket_view.py::list_by_query`), so\nthey can drift.\n\nThis is the prerequisite for the response-budget bound on `daughterly-agitative-ocelot`\n(`494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0`): without this projection a 90,000-byte bound would refuse even\n`list_tickets(status=\"open\")` (51 rows, 224,610 lean bytes). It is independently valuable\nwithout that bound and lands first.\n\n## Blast radius — every consumer of the lean path, enumerated and measured\n\n`lean_projection` is reached only from `list_states` and `TicketView.list_by_query`, and only\nwhen `include_body` is False. `TicketQuery.include_body` defaults **True**\n(`_engine_support/ticket_query.py:52`), so a call that does not ask for lean is unaffected.\nThe six call sites, verified by reading each:\n\n| # | consumer | how it builds the query | narrows? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | CLI `rebar list` (`reads_cli.py:344`) | `include_body = ns.full` (`:286`), i.e. False by default | **YES — default narrows** |\n| 2 | library `rebar.list_tickets` (`_lib_reads.py:166`) | `include_body=full`, `full` defaults False | **YES — default narrows** |\n| 3 | MCP `list_tickets` (`_mcp_reads.py`) | forwards `full` to (2) | **YES — via (2)** |\n| 4 | MCP `ready_tickets` (`_mcp_reads.py:377`) | `rebar.ready(sort=...)`, no `include_body` plumbing | **YES — new, see below** |\n| 5 | `_engine_support/validate.py:67` | `list_states(tracker)` — `query=None` builds a default `TicketQuery()` | NO — `include_body=True` |\n| 6 | `_engine_support/next_batch.py:144` | `TicketQuery(status=\"open,in_progress\")` — `include_body` unset | NO — `include_body=True` |\n\n(5) reduces 2,863 rows and (6) 62 rows; both keep all four fields, so neither the repo-health\nvalidator nor conflict-aware batching loses input. `show_state` and `search_state`\n(`reads.py:338`, `:527`) do not call `list_states` at all — `search` has its own\n`project_search_result` projection — so `show`, `rebar show`, `show_ticket` and `search` are\nuntouched on every surface.\n\nThree surfaces therefore narrow: CLI `rebar list`, MCP `list_tickets`, MCP `ready_tickets`.\n\n## `ready_tickets`: the default narrows, deliberately\n\nOn `origin/main` `ready_tickets(sort)` returns the FULL shape with no opt-out, so a lean\ndefault narrows a published, schema-pinned MCP read. Three options were live:\n\n- **(a) keep the full default, add `full` as an opt-IN to lean.** Rejected: it leaves the two\n  discovery surfaces disagreeing on their default shape for no benefit to any caller, and it\n  strands `ready_tickets` at 693,556 bytes for 61 rows — the single largest unbounded read on\n  the surface.\n- **(b) narrow the default, add `full=True` as the opt-OUT, document the break.** CHOSEN.\n- **(c) leave `ready_tickets` alone entirely.** Rejected for the same reason as (a).\n\nThe library is deliberately NOT changed: `rebar.ready(*, sort, repo_root)` ->\n`ready_states(tracker, *, epic, sort)` -> `public_state` has no `include_body`/`full` plumbing\nand this story adds none. The projection happens one layer up in the MCP tool, through the\nSAME `lean_projection`, so the two discovery surfaces cannot return different shapes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] **One shared projection.** `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` + `lean_projection` in\n      `_engine_support/reads.py` are the only spelling of the lean row, dropping\n      `authorship_ledger`, `attestations`, `signature`, `keyring` as well as `description` and\n      `comments`. Both backends call it: `list_states` and\n      `_snapshot/ticket_view.py::TicketView.list_by_query`.\n- [ ] **Parity is TESTED, not asserted.** Tests against a real pinned view over a real tracker\n      run the same `TicketQuery` through both backends and assert identical key sets (kills\n      \"one backend stopped projecting\"), and assert `include_body=True` still carries the\n      bodies on both (kills \"a backend projects unconditionally\").\n- [ ] **`ready_tickets` gains `full: bool = False`**, projecting through `lean_projection`;\n      `full=True` returns exactly the previous bytes. No library signature changes.\n- [ ] **The CLI drift probe is repaired and stays a drift detector.**\n      `scripts/probe_rebar.py:552` asserts the exact symmetric difference between `rebar show`\n      and `rebar list` key sets in both directions; widening the drop set changes `rebar list`,\n      so the probe must be updated. Its expectation is DERIVED (show-only computed fields, plus\n      the lean-dropped set INTERSECTED with what `show` actually emits) rather than hardcoded,\n      because `authorship_ledger`/`attestations` materialise only once a ticket has signature\n      material — an empty tracker's `show` carries neither.\n- [ ] **All three narrowing surfaces are recorded as pre-1.0 breaking changes** in\n      `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`, each with measured before/after and the\n      opt-out. CLI `rebar list --status closed` (2,696 rows) is measured explicitly because it\n      is a USER-visible change, not an agent-only one.\n- [ ] **Mutation-checked.** Shrinking `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` back to the two body fields must\n      turn the shape tests and the probe RED.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- `make lint` (ruff check + format-check + complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0`),\n  `make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit tests/interfaces` green.\n- `python scripts/probe_rebar.py` green (it was 141/1 before the repair).\n- Change pushed to Gerrit, `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- The MCP response-size bound, `_mcp_budget.py`, and the `response_too_large` refusal — those\n  are `494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0`, which depends on this.\n- A narrower discovery-specific output model — that is `lucky-egoistic-akitainu`\n  (`0c99-8f2b-0de7-48f2`).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS + lean_projection: the ONE spelling of the lean list row, now dropping the signature material as well as the two bodies."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py","reason":"Snapshot read backend calls the same lean_projection so the two backends cannot drift."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"ready_tickets gains full: bool = False and projects through the shared lean_projection via the new _discovery_rows helper; list_tickets docstring records the widened drop set."},{"path":"scripts/probe_rebar.py","reason":"The show-vs-list key-set drift assertion is derived from the lean drop set rather than hardcoded, because widening it narrows CLI rebar list too."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py","reason":"Backend parity tests: same query through both backends, identical key sets; include_body=True still carries the bodies on both."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py","reason":"New: the lean-shape regression tests for list_tickets and ready_tickets over a real store."},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"Pre-1.0 breaking-change note for the three narrowing surfaces with measured before/after."},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"Same breaking change recorded in the curated changelog."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","scale","reads"],"ticket_id":"98b8-5f08-1569-45cc","ticket_type":"story","title":"Make the lean discovery row actually lean: one shared projection across both read backends","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["acd534df-7330-4db8-9066-ea95107b5d5e","ed7cc4a4-a4fa-4303-ab98-41500b5f3ba7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787956864593704401,"uuid":"6fb2aab7-f100-49c1-b0ca-1c81279f2fcb"}